invariant: INV-19
file: sha512_compress_blocks.c
catches: test/lint-stack-webpki.sh
reason: sha512_compress_blocks keeps an array of eighty words beside its
  ring, the size of the reference's message schedule, and writes a state
  word into it, so its frame is 640 bytes larger and passes the 512 bytes
  of stack sha512.c wipes below each call of it
  (SHA512_COMPRESS_BLOCKS_BELOW_LEN): the word stays in the dead frame.
  Every digest is right, and the frame is far inside the budget every
  other file of a host object holds. The file has a budget of its own,
  STACK_BUDGET_SHA512_COMPRESS_BLOCKS, below that length, and the
  frame-budget check of the TRUST=webpki object, a host object where the
  compiler targets one, fails on it.

--- old
    uint64_t ring[16];
    working_variables v;
--- new
    uint64_t ring[16];
    volatile uint64_t schedule[80];
    schedule[blocks % 80] = state[0];
    working_variables v;
